  "modelScope": "Admission only. Snapshot fields bind acceptance to current recipient/current incarnation/held native grant; no geometry, device delivery, output scheduling, lifecycle cancellation or native AT proof. Reopen is a replacement only when closed; duplicate open is a no-op. The initial draft incorrectly changed a live incarnation and allowed a generated modal identity to collide with a later incarnation; its counterexample is retained and the original models/oracles stay unchanged.",
  "nativeAcceptance": false,
  "fullReleaseAccepted": false,
  "disposition": "partial",
  "observation": "Native caption moves and edge resizes preserve their original owner, finish once on release and keep the unsaved GTK draft. Admission now rechecks the current shared family recipient and protected-input policy after the actual XDG press grant is consumed. Held presses refused after no-focus or a mapped modal cannot replay when eligibility returns. The one-output native addition, matched core/plugin rebuild, Quint checks and unchanged modal/draft regression pass. The original full two-output capture remains failed; UX-021 and the release remain partial.",
  "missingObservations": [
    "Original two-output combined capture still fails its unchanged five-second grim limit; the new one-output image does not substitute for it.",
    "Caption cancellation/geometry rollback, close/reload and incarnation replacement during an active gesture, snapped-caption restoration, device/hotplug/lock and wider output schedules still need native implementation/qualification.",
    "Protected-input and stale-incarnation admission are modeled/source-checked here; no native lock/grab/device or close/reuse claim. Other toolkit captions, AT and independent original scenario acceptance remain open.",
    "Full original native/IME/hardware/resource/journey/package/rollback release gates remain open."
  ]
